  <div class="page-divider">Results and Conclusion</div>

  <h3 class="sec-title">12. Results</h3>
  <p>
    The following sample outputs illustrate how the system presents food waste prediction and preparation advisories based on holdout evaluation data.
  </p>

  <table class="custom-table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th style="width: 45%;">Output Metric</th>
        <th style="width: 55%;">Illustrative Result</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><b>Total Meal Sessions Analyzed</b></td><td>450 days (1,350 meal sessions)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Best Performing Model</b></td><td>Gradient Boosting Regressor</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Model Mean Absolute Error (MAE)</b></td><td>1.84 kg</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Model Root Mean Squared Error (RMSE)</b></td><td>2.45 kg</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Model Coefficient of Determination (R²)</b></td><td>0.9412</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Top Influential Factors</b></td><td>Food Prepared (kg), Dish Popularity Rating, Estimated Diners, Session Status</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Average Food Waste per Meal (Unoptimized)</b></td><td>14.8 kg (11.2% leftover ratio)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Sample High-Popularity Lunch (510 diners)</b></td><td>Unoptimized Prep: 280.0 kg | Recommended Prep: 271.8 kg | Waste Saved: 8.2 kg</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Sample Low-Popularity Dinner (380 diners)</b></td><td>Unoptimized Prep: 152.0 kg | Recommended Prep: 122.5 kg | Waste Saved: 29.5 kg</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Estimated Cost Savings per Session</b></td><td>₹ 530.00 – ₹ 1,910.00</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p>
    These results demonstrate that the system accurately captures demand shifts. In sessions with less popular dishes or weekend departures, the model alerts managers to curb over-preparation, reducing waste by up to 20%–25% without risking food shortages.
  </p>

  <h3 class="sec-title">13. Advantages</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Reduces Food Wastage:</b> Prevents tens of kilograms of edible food from ending up in landfills each week.</li>
    <li><b>Cost Savings:</b> Significantly curtails unnecessary expenditure on raw kitchen supplies and catering overheads.</li>
    <li><b>Data-Driven Kitchen Planning:</b> Replaces arbitrary cook guesswork with scientific demand and popularity modeling.</li>
    <li><b>Protects Student Satisfaction:</b> Dynamic safety buffers guarantee students are not left unfed during peak-attendance sessions.</li>
    <li><b>Continuous Improvement:</b> Shift logging functionality establishes a continuous feedback loop for periodic model retraining.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3 class="sec-title">14. Applications</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><b>University and College Hostel Messes:</b> Tailor daily batch sizes according to exam timetables, weekends, and seasonal breaks.</li>
    <li><b>Corporate Office Canteens:</b> Optimize meal preparation around hybrid-work schedules and fluctuating in-office attendance.</li>
    <li><b>Hospital and Healthcare Catering:</b> Predict patient and staff dietary meal requirements with minimum food disposal.</li>
    <li><b>Event and Buffet Catering Services:</b> Estimate required quantities based on RSVP numbers, event types, and dish selections.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3 class="sec-title">15. Limitations</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Sudden Unrecorded Events:</b> Unscheduled campus holidays, sudden student strikes, or external food delivery spikes cannot be anticipated without manual inputs.</li>
    <li><b>Data Quality Dependency:</b> Accuracy relies on faithful reporting of actual diner attendance and discarded leftovers.</li>
    <li><b>Cook Discipline:</b> Recommendations are advisory; kitchen staff must adhere to the suggested weights during batch preparation.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3 class="sec-title">16. Future Scope</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Automated Computer Vision Leftover Weighing:</b> Integrate IoT load cells or smart camera bins to automate waste logging.</li>
    <li><b>Student Mobile App Token System:</b> Integrate with a student app allowing hostelers to tap "Skip Meal" or RSVP 4 hours in advance.</li>
    <li><b>Per-Ingredient Procurement Optimization:</b> Extend models from dish-level weights (kg) to raw ingredient supply chain ordering (rice, vegetables, oil).</li>
    <li><b>Deep Learning Sequence Models:</b> Incorporate Temporal Fusion Transformers (TFT) or LSTM networks for complex multi-term seasonal forecasting.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3 class="sec-title">17. Conclusion</h3>
  <p>
    The AI-Powered Food Waste Prediction and Kitchen Advisory System demonstrates a complete, reviewable approach to transforming institutional canteen management. By combining feature preprocessing, ensemble machine learning regressors, and prescriptive dynamic buffer logic, the system effectively bridges the gap between passive predictive modeling and active kitchen decision support. The accompanying Streamlit interface makes actionable insights accessible to canteen managers, delivering measurable reductions in wasted food, reduced operational budgets, and a more sustainable campus food environment.
  </p>

